WEBVTT

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:21.230
Father“.

00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.234
Luscinia!

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:29.155
You <i>will</i> pay for this...!

00:00:29.405 --> 00:00:33.326
If it is your wish to kill me, Princess, then do so.

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:39.832
But killing me here will not end the war.

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:43.294
The resulting power struggle for
the title of Federation Premier

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:47.924
will engulf foreign lands and
lead to even further chaos.

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:54.347
Humanity does not yet possess the ability

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:59.894
to put an end to its own
chain of cyclical revenge.

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:09.487
Even so, if you are confident you can
rule and establish peace over all...

00:01:09.737 --> 00:01:16.577
...then I ask you to save this
forsaken world in my place.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:37.848
<i>No matter what might await us there</i>

00:01:38.099 --> 00:01:46.524
<i>I'll go to unexplored territory with you</i>

00:01:54.782 --> 00:02:02.832
<i>I just had a short dream</i>

00:02:03.082 --> 00:02:07.461
<i>In it, I saw your back</i>

00:02:07.712 --> 00:02:13.634
<i>Was it the past? The future?</i>

00:02:13.884 --> 00:02:24.395
<i>Ignore the needle on that meter
pointing to the red zone</i>

00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:27.523
<i>And go where the tailwinds
and your feelings point you</i>

00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:33.696
<i>Every time I flap my wings, it makes me realize</i>

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:39.243
<i>That there are skies
I'll never be able to see again</i>

00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:44.749
<i>But if you still want to take flight</i>

00:02:44.999 --> 00:02:51.547
<i>Then I will be your wings</i>

00:03:58.823 --> 00:04:00.366
Sister...

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:03.994
<i>I was so oblivious to everything.</i>

00:04:04.245 --> 00:04:05.996
<i>I never knew about your point of view</i>

00:04:06.247 --> 00:04:08.916
<i>or the fate you were forced to bear...</i>

00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:13.170
<i>Did you endure this weight all this time?</i>

00:04:13.421 --> 00:04:16.006
<i>These inherited memories of a "Key"...</i>

00:04:17.425 --> 00:04:20.052
<i>People always repeat the same mistakes</i>

00:04:20.302 --> 00:04:23.097
<i>and end up tormented by the same despair...</i>

00:04:23.347 --> 00:04:26.434
Always... Always...

00:04:26.684 --> 00:04:28.269
Always...

00:04:31.063 --> 00:04:35.109
<i>Even so, you sacrificed
yourself to become a witch,</i>

00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:38.446
<i>enduring this suffering all the while?</i>

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:55.254
I'm so stupid.

00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:57.590
I didn't understand it at all.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.134
I thought if everyone could just get along,

00:05:00.384 --> 00:05:05.723
all the hate would go away and
then there'd be world peace...

00:05:21.989 --> 00:05:24.200
Don't worry so much, Dyan.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.578
It's a shame you didn't get Luscinia...

00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:32.708
...but that witch was our
motherland's mortal enemy.

00:05:32.958 --> 00:05:39.298
You've done well. We've gotten our revenge.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.520
Revenge...

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:56.357
Yes. You're a hero.

00:05:56.607 --> 00:06:04.698
Then... why don't I feel
the least bit of happiness?

00:06:04.782 --> 00:06:08.202
I am sorry for what happened to Liliana.

00:06:09.245 --> 00:06:13.749
I truly regret that the hope for
a truce has ended in this manner.

00:06:13.999 --> 00:06:18.712
You knew it would turn out this way
from the very start, didn't you?!

00:06:18.963 --> 00:06:21.006
You accepted the truce so easily

00:06:21.257 --> 00:06:24.510
because you knew it would fall right apart!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.930
I had hoped it would not end this way.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:34.520
I wished, just as you did, that it
would lead to true world peace.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:37.106
However...

00:06:37.356 --> 00:06:39.692
...I knew it was not to be.

00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:42.987
It's truly a shame.

00:06:47.783 --> 00:06:50.160
Be there to support Princess Millia.

00:06:50.411 --> 00:06:52.830
That is Liliana's wish.

00:06:54.248 --> 00:06:59.628
If you wanted peace too, then why
did you go and start a war?!

00:06:59.878 --> 00:07:05.134
Because I felt it was necessary.
What else do you think I could have done?

00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:11.849
You, too, should do what you feel is necessary.

00:07:20.232 --> 00:07:24.445
Stopping now would make
Liliana's sacrifice meaningless.

00:07:24.695 --> 00:07:25.571
Yes.

00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:30.784
This is our atonement for surviving
on that day ten years ago.

00:07:34.455 --> 00:07:36.457
We will proceed as planned.

00:07:36.707 --> 00:07:41.462
Should one of us fall,
the other will continue to the end.

00:07:55.726 --> 00:07:58.979
The 1st and 2nd Fleets are departing already?

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:01.857
No, I haven't heard anything about this.

00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:04.526
Have the 2nd Fleet take the lead.

00:08:04.777 --> 00:08:08.864
We will guard the rear and keep
the volunteer forces in check.

00:08:09.114 --> 00:08:11.700
Counterattack at once, should they strike.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.410
Yes, Sir!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.915
Sounds like the Urbanus won't
arrive for a few more days.

00:08:18.165 --> 00:08:19.416
He's off to a late start.

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:22.628
This truce business has become a bit messy...

00:08:22.878 --> 00:08:24.129
What would you do?

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:27.132
Whatever happens happens.

00:08:29.802 --> 00:08:31.095
Bridge here.

00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:33.764
All of Luscinia's fleets are on the move!

00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:36.642
They didn't give any advance notice--!

00:08:45.484 --> 00:08:47.236
Sh-Shouldn't we stop them?!

00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:49.571
We haven't been ordered to attack yet!

00:08:49.822 --> 00:08:53.784
Luscinia will have his way if we let them go now!

00:08:54.034 --> 00:08:57.121
<i>So the truce has fallen apart...</i>

00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:04.586
Don't attack until we've
learned their true intentions.

00:09:04.837 --> 00:09:05.921
Where's firang?

00:09:06.171 --> 00:09:08.757
He's on his way to the Admiraly.

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:11.218
Get the fleet ready to sally ASAP.

00:09:11.468 --> 00:09:14.012
But make <i>very</i> sure we don't open fire.

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:15.764
Yes, Sir!

00:09:16.014 --> 00:09:19.768
<i>You're not even going to mourn her, Luscinia?!</i>

00:09:24.064 --> 00:09:26.275
Vasant!

00:09:26.525 --> 00:09:28.110
What's happened?

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:32.948
It's all right. You've nothing
to worry about, Augusta.

00:09:33.198 --> 00:09:36.952
Things may become a bit turbulent, however,

00:09:37.202 --> 00:09:39.037
so it would be best if you move to a ship--

00:09:39.288 --> 00:09:40.372
No!

00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:44.710
Please! Tell me what's really happening!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:49.214
I know that I'm still a child and I
might not be able to understand...

00:09:49.465 --> 00:09:51.091
But I'll do everything I can!

00:09:51.341 --> 00:09:55.804
I'm the... I'm the Augusta, after all!

00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:57.347
Augusta...

00:09:57.598 --> 00:10:00.517
I can't stand everyone getting hurt and dying

00:10:00.768 --> 00:10:03.645
while I'm left in the dark the entire time!

00:10:03.896 --> 00:10:05.481
So, please!

00:10:09.985 --> 00:10:13.238
I offer my deepest apologies, Augusta.

00:10:13.489 --> 00:10:15.073
Vasant...

00:10:15.324 --> 00:10:19.161
Gloria, Augusta. I am at your mercy.

00:10:19.411 --> 00:10:21.288
I will now--

00:10:30.547 --> 00:10:33.383
I've come to collect you, Augusta.

00:10:33.634 --> 00:10:34.551
Don't move!

00:10:34.802 --> 00:10:36.386
Someone! Stop him!

00:10:36.637 --> 00:10:38.180
It's no use.

00:10:40.098 --> 00:10:44.061
Have you forgotten what I am?

00:10:55.322 --> 00:10:57.825
Come, Augusta.

00:10:59.409 --> 00:11:01.620
Luscinia!

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:29.147
Augusta Sira"...

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.530
Luscinia...?!

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.866
All his fleets are on the move.

00:11:39.116 --> 00:11:42.077
They're ignoring all of our fleet's hails.

00:11:42.327 --> 00:11:45.789
What about Lady Vasant?
Has she issued any orders?

00:11:46.039 --> 00:11:48.959
Nothing at all. We've lost contact with her.

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:53.589
Everything's so chaotic that we
have no idea what's going on...

00:11:54.631 --> 00:11:56.425
_-This
“Hurry!

00:11:56.508 --> 00:12:00.721
Peace has fallen apart again, after all.

00:12:00.971 --> 00:12:03.307
And it's my fault...

00:12:16.528 --> 00:12:19.364
We have to go on the run again for a while.

00:12:19.615 --> 00:12:21.742
Are you okay, Al?

00:12:21.992 --> 00:12:25.078
<i>Never mind me; are you hurt, Die'?</i>

00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:31.877
Die!

00:12:32.127 --> 00:12:33.712
Stay down!

00:13:06.036 --> 00:13:07.871
Lukia...

00:13:15.337 --> 00:13:18.674
Thanks, AI. You're a life-saver.

00:13:18.924 --> 00:13:22.010
L-I didn't do anything...

00:13:39.444 --> 00:13:42.948
I have retrieved our leader from the traitors.

00:13:43.198 --> 00:13:44.408
Fly the Augusta's flag!

00:13:44.658 --> 00:13:46.785
Gloria, Augusta!

00:13:47.035 --> 00:13:50.372
We can expect immediate pursuit.
I leave it to you.

00:13:50.622 --> 00:13:54.501
I will head north with the Augusta as planned.

00:13:54.751 --> 00:13:57.629
--Ready a high-speed Vanship.
--Yes, Sir!

00:13:58.922 --> 00:14:02.426
I expect this to be the true final battle.

00:14:02.676 --> 00:14:07.723
The world will know true peace,
just as Augusta Farahnéz wished.

00:14:07.973 --> 00:14:08.807
Yes.

00:14:09.057 --> 00:14:14.271
Once this battle is over, I intend
to retire from active service

00:14:14.521 --> 00:14:18.859
and let Augusta Sire“! and the
youngsters take care of the rest.

00:14:19.109 --> 00:14:21.236
Admiral. I offer my utmost appreciation.

00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:23.488
It is too soon for gratitude.

00:14:23.739 --> 00:14:27.451
Save it for now, until everything is over.

00:14:27.701 --> 00:14:29.202
Yes.

00:14:42.132 --> 00:14:43.759
Alauda...

00:14:53.727 --> 00:14:59.107
The premier will return with the
power to bring peace to the world!

00:14:59.357 --> 00:15:04.780
Rain justice upon the traitors
who sought to corrupt the Augusta!

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.740
Gloria, Augusta!

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.451
--Gloria, Augusta!
--Gloria, Augusta!

00:15:12.496 --> 00:15:15.874
Th-The Impetus is flying the Augusta's flag!

00:15:16.124 --> 00:15:17.584
Luscinia...

00:15:17.834 --> 00:15:21.630
How many times must you trample
on Augusta Sérifs wishes?!

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.632
We must rescue the Augusta!

00:15:23.882 --> 00:15:25.425
Full speed ahead!

00:15:37.771 --> 00:15:39.856
Lady Vasant...

00:15:45.195 --> 00:15:48.698
I'm gonna go too! I <i>will</i> save Siri!

00:15:48.949 --> 00:15:52.035
I'll remain here and get everything in order!

00:15:52.285 --> 00:15:55.288
We at least need to reestablish
a chain of command!

00:15:59.876 --> 00:16:01.336
Millia!

00:16:03.839 --> 00:16:05.632
I'm sorry, Millia.

00:16:05.882 --> 00:16:10.679
I never once stopped to
think about how you feel.

00:16:10.929 --> 00:16:14.558
Dyan's pain, your suffering...

00:16:14.808 --> 00:16:16.268
I never considered it.

00:16:16.518 --> 00:16:19.563
No, I never even tried to consider it.

00:16:19.813 --> 00:16:21.898
I forced everything onto you,

00:16:22.149 --> 00:16:25.694
even though you were
hurting so much already...

00:16:25.944 --> 00:16:28.238
Just like with Dyan.

00:16:28.488 --> 00:16:33.368
Yet, I went and forced my dream onto you.

00:16:33.618 --> 00:16:37.247
All I cared about was holding a Grand Race...

00:16:37.497 --> 00:16:40.167
I never even tried to figure out

00:16:40.417 --> 00:16:43.628
how to make a Grand Race
possible for everyone,

00:16:43.879 --> 00:16:47.132
or how to make even wanting
one possible for everyone.

00:16:49.843 --> 00:16:51.428
So... I'm sorry.

00:16:51.678 --> 00:16:54.389
I know it doesn't matter now,
but I just wanted to say I'm sorry!

00:16:55.849 --> 00:16:57.309
Wait!

00:16:59.769 --> 00:17:02.063
I'm sorry I didn't give it back sooner.

00:17:07.402 --> 00:17:08.445
Fam.

00:17:08.695 --> 00:17:12.949
I only made it this far thanks to you.

00:17:15.368 --> 00:17:18.872
Your dream was what gave me hope.

00:17:19.122 --> 00:17:22.000
Had it not been for that,
I would've given up long ago

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.046
and abandoned my dream
of rebuilding my homeland.

00:17:28.757 --> 00:17:33.845
Let's make the Grand Race a reality! For sure!

00:17:34.095 --> 00:17:35.680
Millia...

00:17:39.768 --> 00:17:41.853
Don't forget about me!

00:17:42.103 --> 00:17:45.774
No matter what happens down the road,
our dream will never change.

00:17:46.024 --> 00:17:48.318
--Right!
--Yeah!

00:18:08.296 --> 00:18:09.798
Charge formation!

00:18:10.048 --> 00:18:12.926
Lay waste to the enemy!

00:18:16.304 --> 00:18:20.392
Just how far must you trample on our cause?!

00:18:57.929 --> 00:18:59.472
Vasant...

00:18:59.723 --> 00:19:02.392
What happened to Vasant?

00:19:02.642 --> 00:19:06.271
I welcome your return to the Grand Exile...

00:19:06.521 --> 00:19:08.315
...Maestro Sire-l.

00:19:08.565 --> 00:19:10.233
Maestro?

00:19:10.483 --> 00:19:12.944
It is all to save the world...

00:19:13.194 --> 00:19:17.782
To make the peaceful world
Augusta Farahnéz desired a reality.

00:19:20.368 --> 00:19:23.288
That which sleeps in the land of snow...

00:19:23.538 --> 00:19:27.000
A distant promise that guides the lost.

00:19:29.794 --> 00:19:32.005
The vast ocean of stars...

00:19:32.255 --> 00:19:35.925
A far-reaching path of the departed.

00:19:36.176 --> 00:19:38.595
The dream delivered by angels of war...

00:19:38.845 --> 00:19:42.307
A symbol of hope and life:

00:19:42.557 --> 00:19:44.684
the Grand Exile.

00:19:44.934 --> 00:19:47.145
At the far ends of the wish...

00:19:47.395 --> 00:19:51.733
...lie snow-white wings surpassing all.

00:20:04.662 --> 00:20:08.291
Those who've desecrated
the Augusta's wishes must pay!

00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:10.502
Our cause is just!

00:20:12.337 --> 00:20:15.173
Only our leader can have a "cause"!

00:20:15.423 --> 00:20:18.093
Our duty is to serve as her obedient swords!

00:20:26.393 --> 00:20:28.144
Don't let a single ship through.

00:20:28.395 --> 00:20:30.480
All ships, continue to counter!

00:20:37.821 --> 00:20:39.823
<i>Sire-um!</i>

00:20:40.073 --> 00:20:44.202
Let us go forth, abandoning
the ancient land of strife.

00:20:44.452 --> 00:20:47.997
Bountiful skies, everlasting seas.

00:20:48.248 --> 00:20:49.999
I pray for good tailwinds

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:54.421
to carry the wings of the beloved
child bound for a new world.

00:20:54.671 --> 00:20:57.382
Good tailwinds.

00:21:00.885 --> 00:21:03.513
Claudia Unit is down! Helm inoperable!

00:21:03.763 --> 00:21:05.807
Rapidly losing altitude!

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:09.561
Target the 3rd Fleet's flagship, the Admiraly!

00:21:09.811 --> 00:21:12.355
It's time to put an end to the root of our trouble!

00:21:28.621 --> 00:21:30.206
Fire!

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:44.262
What is th--?!

00:22:03.907 --> 00:22:07.410
Never mind me. ls everyone all right?

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.120
Yes, Sir!

00:24:02.692 --> 00:24:05.653
<i>Your Majesty. We will arrive
at the skirmish point shortly.</i>

00:24:05.903 --> 00:24:08.823
<i>Failure in this battle is not an option.</i>

00:24:09.073 --> 00:24:12.827
<i>Understood! I shall risk life and limb so
that we may survive this battle together!</i>

00:24:13.077 --> 00:24:16.122
<i>All forces, Type 1 battle stations!
All ships, full speed ahead!</i>

00:24:16.372 --> 00:24:17.123
<i>As you wish!</i>

00:24:17.373 --> 00:24:18.458
--Vince.
--Your Majesty?

00:24:18.708 --> 00:24:22.378
<i>Do these people know who we are?</i>

00:24:22.629 --> 00:24:27.050
<i>A-All hands to Type 1 battle stations!
All ships, full speed ahead!</i>
